    "raw": "## Question\n\nWould it be worthwhile to extract a common CLI framework (`XXXCommand` ABC: parser fragment + action + optional verify) shared by manage, todo, voxtool, shadup, and upcoming onboardctl?\n\n## Code survey (2026-07-25)\n\n| Tool | Path | Pattern | ABC? |\n|------|------|---------|------|\n| **todo** | `skills/projectmanagement/todos/todo.py` (~4k LOC) | `TodoSubCommand(ABC)`: `command_names`, `configure_parser`, `do()`, `register()`; `COMMAND_CLASSES` loop in `build_parser()` | **Yes -- only full example** |\n| **manage** | `thermo/dmz/manage.py` | Manual `argv[0]` / `if action == ...` dispatch; `_cmd_*` helpers; **no argparse subparsers** | No |\n| **voxtool** | `vox2stl/voxtool.py` | argparse `add_subparsers` + `set_defaults(func=run_*)` free functions | No |\n| **shadup** | `shadup/shadup.py` (~3k LOC) | argparse subparsers; action dispatch on `args.action` | No |\n| **dedup** | `dedup/dedup.py` | Flag modes, not a rich subcommand registry | No |\n| **bff** | sibling `bin/bff.py` | argparse subparsers, procedural `main` | No |\n| **metatool** | sibling `bin/musicology/metatool.py` | argparse subparsers | No |\n| **onboardctl** | planned (todo:a3fce7c0) | Spec asks for ABC + subclasses like todo | Intended |\n\n### Consistency verdict\n\nWe are **not** consistent. The aspirational pattern (ABC + per-subcommand parser/action/verify) exists almost only in **todo**. Everyone else uses either bare argv switches (manage) or argparse + functions (voxtool/shadup/bff). None of the non-todo tools expose a separate \"verification\" hook on the command object; todo's ABC stops at `configure_parser` + `do`.\n\n### What a shared framework would need (thin)\n\nSuggested minimal surface (inspired by `TodoSubCommand`, without todo-specific EDIT/repo coupling):\n\n- `Command` ABC: `names`, `help`, `configure_parser(parser)`, `run(args) -> int`\n- `register_all(subparsers, classes)`\n- Optional later: `verify(args)` / dry-run; undo hint printer (onboardctl wants this)\n\nPlacement candidates: `utils/lib/` or small package under `extdeps/` consumable by utils + bin.\n\n### Worth it? (survey recommendation)\n\n| Factor | Note |\n|--------|------|\n| Greenfield | **Yes-ish** -- onboardctl and future CLIs benefit from copying a 50-line base instead of inventing a third style. |\n| Migrate manage/voxtool/shadup now | **Probably no** -- large procedural CLIs; rewrite cost >> consistency gain unless already mid-touch. |\n| Extract from todo.py | **Careful** -- todo's base is entangled with EDIT sentinel, gitroot, logging; extract a *thin* sibling, do not drag todo into a shared package overnight. |\n| Verify hook | Not present today; only add if onboardctl/manage dry-run needs it. |\n\n**Lean recommendation:** extract a tiny optional `cli_command` helper for *new* tools (start with onboardctl); leave existing CLIs alone until each is next edited. Revisit a manage/voxtool migration only if two+ rewrites land in one quarter.\n\n## Non-goals for this ticket\n\nDo not implement the framework here. This todo is the survey + decision record; implementation is a follow-on if AC says proceed."
  },
